<!DOCTYPE language>
<!--
  Objective-C (Monal)

  Plain "Objective-C" plus
   * the MLHandler macro language (MLHandler.h)
     https://github.com/monal-im/Monal/wiki/Handler-Framework
   * the XML query language, but only in string literals passed to the MLXMLNode
     selectors find: findFirst: and check: (everything else stays a normal ObjC string)
     https://github.com/monal-im/Monal/wiki/XML-Query-Language
   * SQLite in string literals consumed by MLSQLite: passed to one of its execute*:
     selectors (or internalExecuteScalar: / prepareQuery:), or assigned (`= @"...`) when
     the literal starts with an SQL statement keyword (NSString* query = @"SELECT ...").
     Multiline strings (backslash-newline continuation) are supported.
     SQL rules are reused from Kate's generic "SQL" definition, extended by SQLite
     specific keywords, functions and bind parameters.
-->
